--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -30,6 +30,9 @@ Game features, performance improvements, and bug fixes for NFS Carbon in the bro
 - Stop pinch zoom, the long-press menu and page bounce from interrupting play on phones.
 - Stop the game writing to its whole 2 GB memory area at start, which crashed iPhones and used about 1.8 GB more memory on every device.
 - Render phones at a lower resolution and start fewer background workers on touch devices, to use less memory.
+- Treat an iPad like a phone whatever it has attached: with a trackpad or Magic Keyboard, Safari reports a fine pointer and a Macintosh user agent, which skipped the lower resolution, the smaller import buffers and the folder-picker check.
+- Wait for landscape on tablets too, not only on phones: a portrait iPad started the game in a portrait resolution for the whole session.
+- Say in the FAQ and README what an iPad or iPhone needs: Safari on iPadOS or iOS 26, a normal tab, landscape.
 
 - Remove traffic from every race together and from all Drift and Canyon Drift races: each player's traffic exists in their own game alone.
 - Keep other players' cars hidden until everyone has loaded, so nobody sits on the grid looking like a bot.
